      "id": "1d1ntm6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. List of Fundamental Rights"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fundamental Rights are guaranteed to all citizens under Part III (Articles 12–35) of the Indian Constitution.",
        "Right to Equality (Articles 14–18) establishes equality before the law and prohibits discrimination on grounds of religion, race, caste, sex, or place of birth.",
        "Right to Freedom (Articles 19–22) protects key individual freedoms including speech, assembly, and movement, subject to reasonable restrictions.",
        "Right to Constitutional Remedies (Article 32) empowers citizens to approach the Supreme Court directly for the enforcement of Fundamental Rights."
      ],
      "id": "anzmyuh"
    },
