    {
      "id": "9a4vann",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Right to Constitutional Remedies (Articles 32–35)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "39njibj"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The Right to Property (Article 31) was deleted from the list of Fundamental Rights by the 44th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1978, making it a legal right under Article 300A.",
        "Fundamental Rights guaranteed under Articles 20 and 21 cannot be suspended even during a National Emergency.",
        "Article 32 provides for 5 types of writs: Habeas Corpus, Mandamus, Prohibition, Certiorari, and Quo-Warranto."
      ],
      "id": "8g8cvt7"
